Error [E0373]: This explicit semicolon is not part of canonical Jet syntax.
  --> tests/ui/loop_header_semicolon_retired.jet:2:14
    |
  2 |     loop item; [1, 2, 3] { print(item) }
    |              ^
 Why: Jet uses line boundaries for statements; the parser preserves this boundary so the same program can be repaired without changing behavior.
 Fix: Replace the semicolon with a line break when code follows it, or remove it at the end of a line; `jet fmt` applies this fix.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0373
